  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Compact white workspace",
    "overview": "Rein is a compact application for operating a workspace through scoped group conversations and Agent tasks. White work areas, a pale sidebar, gray task groups and small controls keep conversation, task status and execution output visible together. Typography and spacing serve scanning and frequent interaction.\n\nThe visual authority is [Figma pzrgKXgJAyugcvBNC16Ick](https://www.figma.com/design/pzrgKXgJAyugcvBNC16Ick): main workspace `2:34`, task detail `2:35`, login `12:1111`, settings `12:1112`–`12:1116`, account menu `24:3887` and logout dialog `24:4369`. The implemented source of tokens is `src/theme.ts`; `src/App.css` and the components define layout and component details. Preserve these references when extending the application.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Compact white application surfaces with thin dividers.",
      "Small Inter and Noto Sans SC typography; JetBrains Mono for terminal output.",
      "Blue actions and selection, with explicit status text alongside status icons.",
      "Resizable conversation and task panes, with responsive navigation and task groups.",
      "Native Figma SVG assets at their intended intrinsic sizes."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Status Meaning Rule",
        "body": "Keep waiting, execution and completion colors tied to their existing meanings. Accompany status colors with labels or icons.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the pinned Figma nodes and implemented theme as visual authority for new screens.",
      "**Do** preserve the compact type hierarchy, white work areas and gray navigation and task-group surfaces.",
      "**Do** preserve native Figma SVG geometry and existing icon source paths, including the nested logout glyph.",
      "**Do** keep both desktop panes resizable with their minimum widths and persist the user's ratio.",
      "**Do** let stacked task groups grow to their content and switch card columns using task-container width.",
      "**Do** retain visible keyboard focus, labeled controls, status text and reduced-motion behavior."
    ],
    "donts": [
